license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible implementation of Cyber Anathema / Adaptive HQCA for
  classical-quantum intrusion detection, including standard and prospective
  benchmarks, source/attack-family zero-day validation, Classical–Quantum
  Complementarity Shift (CQCS), calibration and threshold-transfer analysis,
  and paired statistical evaluation.
keywords:
  - cyber anathema
  - hybrid quantum-classical learning
  - intrusion detection
  - quantum machine learning
  - zero-day
  - distribution shift
  - complementarity shift
  - calibration
  - threshold transfer
  - out-of-fold fusion
